data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Sort a copy of the data. For q, compute `h = q * (n - 1)`, let `lo = floor(h)`, and interpolate\nbetween `s[lo]` and `s[min(lo + 1, n - 1)]` using `h - lo`. Then `IQR = Q3 - Q1`, and the fences\nare `Q1 - k * IQR` and `Q3 + k * IQR`."},"hints_note":null}

